// J4 — tape-wrinkle
// Performance: low
// Webcam safe: yes
// Preserves alpha: yes
// Use case: VHS/Betamax tape wrinkle — vertical bands of horizontal warp with brightness variation
// Chain order: apply before tracking/noise, after color grading

uniform float4x4 ViewProj;
uniform float wrinkle_scale   = 4.0;  // 1.0 – 10.0   number of vertical wrinkle bands
uniform float warp_amount     = 0.012; // 0.0 – 0.03   max horizontal displacement
uniform float brightness_var  = 0.12; // 0.0 – 0.3    brightness fluctuation along warp

uniform texture2d image;

sampler_state textureSampler {
    Filter   = Linear;
    AddressU = Clamp;
    AddressV = Clamp;
};

struct VertData {
    float4 pos : POSITION;
    float2 uv  : TEXCOORD0;
};


VertData VSDefault(VertData v_in)
{
    VertData vert_out;
    vert_out.pos = mul(float4(v_in.pos.xyz, 1.0), ViewProj);
    vert_out.uv  = v_in.uv;
    return vert_out;
}

// Smooth noise using hash + bilinear blend
float Hash11(float x)
{
    return frac(sin(x * 127.1) * 43758.5453);
}

float Hash21(float2 p)
{
    return frac(sin(dot(p, float2(127.1, 311.7))) * 43758.5453);
}

// Value noise in 1D
float Noise1D(float x)
{
    float i = floor(x);
    float f = frac(x);
    float a = Hash11(i);
    float b = Hash11(i + 1.0);
    float t = f * f * (3.0 - 2.0 * f); // smoothstep
    return lerp(a, b, t);
}

// Two-octave 1D value noise
float SmoothNoise(float x)
{
    return Noise1D(x) * 0.6 + Noise1D(x * 2.37 + 5.3) * 0.3 + Noise1D(x * 5.1 + 11.7) * 0.1;
}

float4 mainImage(VertData v_in) : TARGET
{
    float2 uv = v_in.uv;

    // Wrinkle field: noise over X position, scaled by wrinkle_scale
    float wrinklePos  = uv.x * wrinkle_scale;
    float noiseVal    = SmoothNoise(wrinklePos);   // 0..1
    float warpSigned  = (noiseVal - 0.5) * 2.0;   // -1..1

    // Horizontal displacement proportional to noise
    float dispX = warpSigned * warp_amount;

    // Brightness variation aligned with the warp ridge/valley
    // Bright at peaks, dark at troughs (tape catching light at fold)
    float brightDelta = warpSigned * brightness_var;

    float2 warpedUv = float2(saturate(uv.x + dispX), uv.y);
    float4 col = image.Sample(textureSampler, warpedUv);

    // Apply brightness variation — simulate crinkle light catch
    col.rgb = saturate(col.rgb + brightDelta);

    // Secondary fine wrinkle: very high-frequency crinkle texture overlay
    float fineNoise = Noise1D(uv.x * wrinkle_scale * 8.3 + 42.0);
    float fineDelta = (fineNoise - 0.5) * brightness_var * 0.3;
    col.rgb = saturate(col.rgb + fineDelta);

    return float4(col.rgb, col.a);
}

technique Draw
{
    pass
    {
        vertex_shader = VSDefault(v_in);
        pixel_shader  = mainImage(v_in);
    }
}
